\section{Axiomatic Foundations}

TSSE is built upon four axioms:

\begin{description}
  \item[Axiom 1: Temporal Invariance]
  A temporal symmetry operator $\mathcal{T}$ satisfies $\mathcal{T}^2 = I$ and
  commutes with the Hamiltonian $H$.

  \item[Axiom 2: Phase-Space Conservation]
  The evolution operator $\mathcal{U}(t)$ preserves phase-space volume:
  \[
    \det(D\mathcal{U}(t)) = 1.
  \]

  \item[Axiom 3: Structural Manifold Closure]
  All trajectories remain confined to a closed manifold $\mathcal{S}$:
  \[
    \mathcal{U}(t)\mathcal{S} = \mathcal{S}.
  \]

  \item[Axiom 4: Symplectic Consistency]
  Evolution is symplectic:
  \[
    \mathcal{U}(t)^\top J\,\mathcal{U}(t) = J.
  \]
\end{description}

These axioms define the admissible class of TSSE systems.

